The above covers this package's own source. It does not cover the compiled
artifact it ships: `java_fmt.wasm.br` and `java_fmt.runtime.mjs` embed
google-java-format and Guava (Apache-2.0), the Checker Framework qualifiers
(MIT), TeaVM's class library and runtime (Apache-2.0), and javac's parser from
OpenJDK 21 (GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception).

Those terms, and what they permit - the Classpath Exception is what allows the
artifact to be distributed under terms of your choice, including inside a
product you charge for - are set out in `licenses/NOTICE.md`, with the full
texts alongside it.
